IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`
IMPORT `cpp-core-calendar`
IMPORT `cpp-core-age`
IMPORT `cp3-nouns`

-- Canada Pension Plan Act, Part II -- THE BASIC AMOUNT AND ANNUAL ADJUSTMENT OF A BENEFIT (section 45) AND THE
-- AMOUNT OF A RETIREMENT PENSION (section 46).
--
-- Section 46(1) puts the basic monthly amount of a retirement pension at 25 per cent of the average monthly
-- pensionable earnings plus 8.33 per cent of the first additional and 33.33 per cent of the second additional
-- monthly pensionable earnings. A pension that starts before or after the month of the 65th birthday is raised
-- or cut by a factor (subsections (3) and (3.1)); the Act leaves the factor to the Minister (before 2011) and to
-- regulations (from 2011: regulations 78.3 and 78.4, piece cr2), so it is a plain input here. Section 45(2)
-- then moves the amount with the Pension Index each year.
--
-- Ages go through section 2(2) of the Act (the core's cpp-core-age.l4): "the month in which the contributor
-- reaches 65 years of age" is the first day of the month after the 65th birthday's month.

§ `Part II -- Division B -- basic amount and annual adjustment (section 45)`

-- src:1066 | 45 (1) A reference in this Part to the basic amount of any benefit shall be construed as a reference to the amount thereof calculated as provided in this Part without regard to subsection (2).
@ref Act s 45(1) (src:1066)
GIVEN `the amount of the benefit calculated as provided in this Part, without the annual adjustment of subsection (2)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
-- Plain gloss: "the basic amount" of a benefit is the amount worked out as Part II provides without the yearly
-- adjustment of subsection (2). The rule returns that amount as it is.
`s 45(1) — the basic amount of a benefit` `the amount of the benefit calculated as provided in this Part, without the annual adjustment of subsection (2)` MEANS
    `the amount of the benefit calculated as provided in this Part, without the annual adjustment of subsection (2)`

-- src:1068 | (2) Where any benefit has become payable commencing with a month in any year, the basic monthly amount of the benefit shall be adjusted annually, in prescribed manner, so that the amount payable for a month in any following year is an amount equal to the product obtained by multiplying
-- src:1069 | (a) the amount that would have been payable for that month if no adjustment had been made under this section with respect to that following year,
-- src:1070 | by
-- src:1071 | (b) the ratio that the Pension Index for that following year bears to the Pension Index for the year preceding that following year.
@ref Act s 45(2) (src:1068-1071)
GIVEN `the amount that would have been payable for the month if no adjustment had been made under this section with respect to the following year` IS A NUMBER
      `the Pension Index for the following year` IS A NUMBER
      `the Pension Index for the year preceding the following year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
-- Plain gloss: once a benefit has become payable, the basic monthly amount is adjusted each year: the amount for a
-- month in the following year is the amount that would have been payable for it without that year's adjustment,
-- multiplied by the ratio of the Pension Index of the following year to that of the year before it. The
-- "prescribed manner" is regulation 62 (piece cr2). NOTHING means the earlier Pension Index is zero.
-- out of range: regulation 62 (piece cr2), the "prescribed manner" of the adjustment, which rounds the product to the cent: not done here.
`s 45(2) — the amount payable for a month in the following year after the annual adjustment` `the amount that would have been payable for the month if no adjustment had been made under this section with respect to the following year` `the Pension Index for the following year` `the Pension Index for the year preceding the following year` MEANS
    IF `the Pension Index for the year preceding the following year` EQUALS 0
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (`the amount that would have been payable for the month if no adjustment had been made under this section with respect to the following year` TIMES (`the Pension Index for the following year` DIVIDED BY `the Pension Index for the year preceding the following year`))

-- src:1067 | Annual adjustments
-- src:1068 | (2) Where any benefit has become payable commencing with a month in any year, the basic monthly amount of the benefit shall be adjusted annually, in prescribed manner, so that the amount payable for a month in any following year is an amount equal to the product obtained by multiplying
-- src:1069 | (a) the amount that would have been payable for that month if no adjustment had been made under this section with respect to that following year,
-- src:1070 | by
-- src:1071 | (b) the ratio that the Pension Index for that following year bears to the Pension Index for the year preceding that following year.
@ref Act s 45(2) (src:1067-1071)
GIVEN `the basic monthly amount of the benefit in the year it became payable` IS A NUMBER
      `the Pension Index for the year the benefit became payable, and for each year after it, up to the year asked about` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
-- Plain gloss: the same adjustment year after year: the amount for a month in a later year, from the basic amount
-- of the year the benefit became payable and the Pension Index of every year from then to the year asked about,
-- first year first. Each year's step multiplies by that year's index over the year before's, so the steps carry
-- the basic amount to its amount times the last index over the first. NOTHING means a zero index meets a step.
`s 45(2) — the amount payable for a month in a later year after the annual adjustments` `the basic monthly amount of the benefit in the year it became payable` `the Pension Index for the year the benefit became payable, and for each year after it, up to the year asked about` MEANS
    `adjusted year by year` `the basic monthly amount of the benefit in the year it became payable` `the Pension Index for the year the benefit became payable, and for each year after it, up to the year asked about`
    WHERE
        `adjusted year by year` amount indexes MEANS
            CONSIDER indexes
            WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING
            WHEN earlier FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
                (CONSIDER rest
                 WHEN EMPTY THEN JUST amount
                 WHEN later FOLLOWED BY more THEN
                     (CONSIDER `s 45(2) — the amount payable for a month in the following year after the annual adjustment` amount later earlier
                      WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
                      WHEN JUST adjusted THEN `adjusted year by year` adjusted rest))

§ `Part II -- Division B -- the amount of a retirement pension (section 46)`

-- src:1075 | 46 (1) Subject to this section, a retirement pension payable to a contributor is a basic monthly amount equal to the aggregate of
-- src:1076 | (a) 25% of their average monthly pensionable earnings,
-- src:1077 | (b) 8.33% of their first additional monthly pensionable earnings, and
-- src:1078 | (c) 33.33% of their second additional monthly pensionable earnings.
@ref Act s 46(1) (src:1075-1078)
GIVEN `the average monthly pensionable earnings of the contributor` IS A NUMBER
      `the first additional monthly pensionable earnings of the contributor` IS A NUMBER
      `the second additional monthly pensionable earnings of the contributor` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
-- Plain gloss: the basic monthly amount of a retirement pension is 25% of the average monthly pensionable earnings,
-- plus 8.33% of the first additional monthly pensionable earnings, plus 33.33% of the second additional monthly
-- pensionable earnings. The section is "subject to this section": subsections (2) to (6) change it.
`s 46(1) — the basic monthly amount of a retirement pension` `the average monthly pensionable earnings of the contributor` `the first additional monthly pensionable earnings of the contributor` `the second additional monthly pensionable earnings of the contributor` MEANS
        (25% TIMES `the average monthly pensionable earnings of the contributor`)
    PLUS (8.33% TIMES `the first additional monthly pensionable earnings of the contributor`)
    PLUS (33.33% TIMES `the second additional monthly pensionable earnings of the contributor`)

-- src:1079 | Special case
-- src:1080 | (2) Subject to this section, the portion referred to in paragraph (1)(a) of the basic monthly amount of a retirement pension payable to a former disability pension recipient in respect of whom a division under section 55 or 55.1 is approved either before or after the commencement of the retirement pension, if the division reduces the retirement pension otherwise payable, is calculated by dividing
-- src:1081 | (a) the aggregate of
-- src:1082 | (i) the portion of the basic monthly amount of the retirement pension calculated in accordance with paragraph (1)(a) that would be payable to the contributor had their base unadjusted pensionable earnings not been subject to the division, multiplied by the number of months that have been excluded from the contributor’s contributory period by reason of disability, and
-- src:1083 | (ii) the portion of the basic monthly amount of the retirement pension calculated in accordance with paragraph (1)(a) that would be payable following the division, multiplied by the number of months in the contributor’s contributory period calculated in accordance with section 49
-- src:1084 | by
-- src:1085 | (b) the aggregate of
-- src:1086 | (i) the number of months that have been excluded from the contributor’s contributory period by reason of disability, and
-- src:1087 | (ii) the number of months in the contributor’s contributory period calculated in accordance with section 49.
@ref Act s 46(2) (src:1079-1087)
GIVEN `the contributor is a former disability pension recipient in respect of whom a division under section 55 or 55.1 is approved before or after the commencement of the retirement pension` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the division reduces the retirement pension otherwise payable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the portion calculated in accordance with paragraph (1)(a) that would be payable had the base unadjusted pensionable earnings not been subject to the division` IS A NUMBER
      `the portion calculated in accordance with paragraph (1)(a) that would be payable following the division` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of months excluded from the contributor's contributory period by reason of disability` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of months in the contributor's contributory period calculated in accordance with section 49` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
-- Plain gloss: for a former disability pension recipient whose pension the division reduces, the portion of the
-- retirement pension that comes from the average monthly pensionable earnings is a weighted average of the portion
-- without the division and the portion after it: the first weighted by the months excluded for disability, the second
-- by the months of the contributory period. NOTHING means the subsection does not apply (subsection (1)(a)'s portion
-- stands) or the weights add to zero.
`s 46(2) — the portion of a retirement pension under paragraph (1)(a) for a former disability pension recipient whose pension a division reduces` `the contributor is a former disability pension recipient in respect of whom a division under section 55 or 55.1 is approved before or after the commencement of the retirement pension` `the division reduces the retirement pension otherwise payable` `the portion calculated in accordance with paragraph (1)(a) that would be payable had the base unadjusted pensionable earnings not been subject to the division` `the portion calculated in accordance with paragraph (1)(a) that would be payable following the division` `the number of months excluded from the contributor's contributory period by reason of disability` `the number of months in the contributor's contributory period calculated in accordance with section 49` MEANS
    IF `the contributor is a former disability pension recipient in respect of whom a division under section 55 or 55.1 is approved before or after the commencement of the retirement pension` AND `the division reduces the retirement pension otherwise payable` AND `the total of the months` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN JUST (((`the portion calculated in accordance with paragraph (1)(a) that would be payable had the base unadjusted pensionable earnings not been subject to the division` TIMES `the number of months excluded from the contributor's contributory period by reason of disability`)
                PLUS (`the portion calculated in accordance with paragraph (1)(a) that would be payable following the division` TIMES `the number of months in the contributor's contributory period calculated in accordance with section 49`))
               DIVIDED BY `the total of the months`)
    ELSE NOTHING
    WHERE
        `the total of the months` MEANS `the number of months excluded from the contributor's contributory period by reason of disability` PLUS `the number of months in the contributor's contributory period calculated in accordance with section 49`

-- The time interval, in months, between the month with which a retirement pension commences and the
-- month in which the contributor reached, or would reach, 65 years of age, never taken as more than five years (60
-- months), as subsections (3) and (7) provide. The factors themselves are the Minister's (subsection (3)) or the
-- Governor in Council's (subsections (3.1) and (7)); this is the interval they reflect.
-- src:1089 | (3) Subject to subsections (4) to (6), a retirement pension that becomes payable after December 31, 1986 and before January 1, 2011 commencing with a month other than the month in which the contributor reaches 65 years of age is a basic monthly amount equal to the basic monthly amount calculated in accordance with subsection (1) or (2), as the case may be, adjusted by a factor fixed by the Minister, on the advice of the Chief Actuary of the Office of the Superintendent of Financial Institutions, to reflect the time interval between the month in which the retirement pension commences and the month in which the contributor reached, or would reach, 65 years of age, but the time interval is deemed never to exceed five years.
-- src:1111 | (7) For the purposes of subsection (3.1), the Governor in Council may make regulations fixing one or more adjustment factors or the methods of calculating them — including factors or methods that may apply on specified dates — to reflect the time interval between the month in which the retirement pension commences and the month in which the contributor reached, or would reach, 65 years of age, but the time interval is deemed never to exceed five years.
@ref Act s 46(3), (7) (src:1089), (src:1111)
GIVEN `the month with which the retirement pension commences` IS A DATE
      `the contributor's date of birth` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`cp3 — the time interval between the commencement of a retirement pension and the month of reaching 65, in months, at most five years` `the month with which the retirement pension commences` `the contributor's date of birth` MEANS
    min 60 (`absolute value` (`the number of months from the month of one date to the month of another` `the month with which the retirement pension commences` (`s 2(2) — the date a person is deemed to reach a specified age` `the contributor's date of birth` 65)))
    WHERE
        `absolute value` n MEANS IF n LESS THAN 0 THEN 0 MINUS n ELSE n

-- src:1089 | (3) Subject to subsections (4) to (6), a retirement pension that becomes payable after December 31, 1986 and before January 1, 2011 commencing with a month other than the month in which the contributor reaches 65 years of age is a basic monthly amount equal to the basic monthly amount calculated in accordance with subsection (1) or (2), as the case may be, adjusted by a factor fixed by the Minister, on the advice of the Chief Actuary of the Office of the Superintendent of Financial Institutions, to reflect the time interval between the month in which the retirement pension commences and the month in which the contributor reached, or would reach, 65 years of age, but the time interval is deemed never to exceed five years.
@ref Act s 46(3) (src:1089)
GIVEN `the basic monthly amount calculated in accordance with subsection (1) or (2)` IS A NUMBER
      `the month with which the retirement pension commences` IS A DATE
      `the contributor's date of birth` IS A DATE
      `the factor fixed by the Minister, on the advice of the Chief Actuary of the Office of the Superintendent of Financial Institutions, to reflect the time interval` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
-- Plain gloss: a retirement pension that becomes payable after 31 December 1986 and before 1 January 2011, with a
-- month other than the month the contributor reaches 65, is the basic monthly amount of subsection (1) or (2) times a
-- factor fixed by the Minister to reflect the time interval between the month it commences and the month the
-- contributor reached or would reach 65 (never more than five years). The text gives no factor and the Minister's
-- factor is not among the inputs, so it is a plain input. NOTHING means the subsection does not reach the pension.
-- out of range: the factor is fixed by the Minister on the advice of the Chief Actuary (not among the inputs): taken as a number.
`s 46(3) — the basic monthly amount of a retirement pension that becomes payable after 1986 and before 2011, adjusted by the Minister's factor` `the basic monthly amount calculated in accordance with subsection (1) or (2)` `the month with which the retirement pension commences` `the contributor's date of birth` `the factor fixed by the Minister, on the advice of the Chief Actuary of the Office of the Superintendent of Financial Institutions, to reflect the time interval` MEANS
    IF     `the month with which the retirement pension commences` AT LEAST (YMD 1987 1 1)
       AND `the month with which the retirement pension commences` LESS THAN (YMD 2011 1 1)
       AND (NOT (`the month of a date` `the month with which the retirement pension commences` EQUALS `the month of a date` (`s 2(2) — the date a person is deemed to reach a specified age` `the contributor's date of birth` 65)))
    THEN JUST (`the basic monthly amount calculated in accordance with subsection (1) or (2)` TIMES `the factor fixed by the Minister, on the advice of the Chief Actuary of the Office of the Superintendent of Financial Institutions, to reflect the time interval`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1091 | (3.1) Subject to subsections (4) to (6), a retirement pension that becomes payable after December 31, 2010 commencing with a month other than the month in which the contributor reaches 65 years of age is a basic monthly amount equal to the basic monthly amount calculated in accordance with subsection (1) or (2), as the case may be, adjusted by a factor fixed under subsection (7).
@ref Act s 46(3.1) (src:1091)
GIVEN `the basic monthly amount calculated in accordance with subsection (1) or (2)` IS A NUMBER
      `the month with which the retirement pension commences` IS A DATE
      `the contributor's date of birth` IS A DATE
      `the adjustment factor fixed under subsection (7)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
-- Plain gloss: a retirement pension that becomes payable after 31 December 2010, with a month other than the month the
-- contributor reaches 65, is the basic monthly amount of subsection (1) or (2) times the adjustment factor fixed under
-- subsection (7). Subsection (7) is a power to make regulations; the factors are those of regulations 78.3 and 78.4
-- (piece cr2), so the factor is a plain input. NOTHING means the subsection does not reach the pension.
-- out of range: regulations 78.3 and 78.4 (piece cr2) fix the factor under subsection (7): taken as a number.
`s 46(3.1) — the basic monthly amount of a retirement pension that becomes payable after 2010, adjusted by the factor fixed under subsection (7)` `the basic monthly amount calculated in accordance with subsection (1) or (2)` `the month with which the retirement pension commences` `the contributor's date of birth` `the adjustment factor fixed under subsection (7)` MEANS
    IF     `the month with which the retirement pension commences` AT LEAST (YMD 2011 1 1)
       AND (NOT (`the month of a date` `the month with which the retirement pension commences` EQUALS `the month of a date` (`s 2(2) — the date a person is deemed to reach a specified age` `the contributor's date of birth` 65)))
    THEN JUST (`the basic monthly amount calculated in accordance with subsection (1) or (2)` TIMES `the adjustment factor fixed under subsection (7)`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1093 | (4) Subject to subsection (5), if, as a result of a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings under section 55 or 55.1, a retirement pension that was payable increases, the adjustment factor applicable after the increase to the basic monthly amount of the retirement pension calculated in accordance with subsection (1) or (2), as the case may be, instead of the adjustment factor referred to in subsection (3) or (3.1), as the case may be, shall be determined by the formula
-- src:1094 | [(F1 × P1) + (F2 × E)] / P2
-- src:1095 | where
-- src:1096 | F1 is an amount equal to the adjustment factor referred to in subsection (3) or (3.1), as the case may be, at the time the retirement pension first became payable;
-- src:1097 | P1 is the basic monthly amount of the retirement pension calculated in accordance with subsection (1) or (2), as the case may be, before the division;
-- src:1098 | F2 is the lesser of
-- src:1099 | (a) an amount equal to what the adjustment factor referred to in subsection (3) or (3.1), as the case may be, would have been if the retirement pension had commenced in the month in which the increase commences to be payable, and
-- src:1100 | (b) 1;
-- src:1101 | E is equal to the excess of P2 over P1; and
-- src:1102 | P2 is the basic monthly amount of the retirement pension immediately following the division.
@ref Act s 46(4) (src:1093-1102)
GIVEN `the adjustment factor at the time the retirement pension first became payable (F1)` IS A NUMBER
      `the basic monthly amount before the division (P1)` IS A NUMBER
      `the adjustment factor if the retirement pension had commenced in the month in which the increase commences to be payable` IS A NUMBER
      `the basic monthly amount immediately following the division (P2)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
-- Plain gloss: when a division increases a retirement pension that was already payable, the factor applied after the
-- increase is [(F1 x P1) + (F2 x E)] / P2, where F1 is the factor from the start, P1 the amount before the division,
-- F2 the lesser of 1 and the factor had the pension started in the month the increase commences to be payable, E the
-- excess of P2 over P1 and P2 the amount just after the division. NOTHING means P2 is zero.
`s 46(4) — the adjustment factor applied after a division increases a retirement pension` `the adjustment factor at the time the retirement pension first became payable (F1)` `the basic monthly amount before the division (P1)` `the adjustment factor if the retirement pension had commenced in the month in which the increase commences to be payable` `the basic monthly amount immediately following the division (P2)` MEANS
    IF `the basic monthly amount immediately following the division (P2)` EQUALS 0
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (((`the adjustment factor at the time the retirement pension first became payable (F1)` TIMES `the basic monthly amount before the division (P1)`)
                PLUS ((min `the adjustment factor if the retirement pension had commenced in the month in which the increase commences to be payable` 1) TIMES (`the basic monthly amount immediately following the division (P2)` MINUS `the basic monthly amount before the division (P1)`)))
               DIVIDED BY `the basic monthly amount immediately following the division (P2)`)

-- src:1104 | (5) Unless otherwise provided by an agreement under section 80, if a person receives a retirement pension under this Act and a survivor’s pension under this Act and the survivor’s pension is at any time reduced from its full amount under subsection 58(2), any downward adjustment factor resulting from the application of subsection (3), (3.1) or (4) at that time shall not be applied to the whole of the basic monthly amount of the retirement pension calculated in accordance with subsection (1) or (2), as the case may be, but only to the amount remaining when that basic monthly amount is reduced by the product obtained by multiplying
-- src:1105 | (a) the amount by which the survivor’s pension has been reduced
-- src:1106 | by
-- src:1107 | (b) the ratio that the Pension Index for the year in which the retirement pension first commenced to be payable bears to the Pension Index for the year in which the survivor’s pension is reduced.
@ref Act s 46(5) (src:1104-1107)
GIVEN `an agreement under section 80 provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person receives a retirement pension and a survivor's pension under this Act, and the survivor's pension is reduced from its full amount under subsection 58(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the basic monthly amount of the retirement pension calculated in accordance with subsection (1) or (2)` IS A NUMBER
      `the downward adjustment factor resulting from subsection (3), (3.1) or (4)` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount by which the survivor's pension has been reduced` IS A NUMBER
      `the Pension Index for the year in which the retirement pension first commenced to be payable` IS A NUMBER
      `the Pension Index for the year in which the survivor's pension is reduced` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
-- Plain gloss: unless an agreement under section 80 says otherwise, a person with a retirement pension and a survivor's
-- pension reduced under subsection 58(2) has the downward factor applied only to what remains of the basic monthly amount
-- after taking off the reduction (times the ratio of the two Pension Indexes); the part taken off is not cut by the factor.
-- The text does not say what happens to that part: it is read as paid at the basic amount, so the total is
-- (basic - X) x factor + X, with X the reduction carried by the Pension Index ratio (NOTES.md, fork register).
-- NOTHING means the subsection does not apply (the factor is not a downward one, no reduction, or an agreement) or an index is zero.
-- out of range: subsection 58(2) (piece cp4) reduces the survivor's pension, and section 80 (piece cp5) allows an agreement that provides otherwise: both are taken as facts.
`s 46(5) — the basic monthly amount of a retirement pension when the factor is applied only to the amount left after a survivor's pension reduction` `an agreement under section 80 provides otherwise` `the person receives a retirement pension and a survivor's pension under this Act, and the survivor's pension is reduced from its full amount under subsection 58(2)` `the basic monthly amount of the retirement pension calculated in accordance with subsection (1) or (2)` `the downward adjustment factor resulting from subsection (3), (3.1) or (4)` `the amount by which the survivor's pension has been reduced` `the Pension Index for the year in which the retirement pension first commenced to be payable` `the Pension Index for the year in which the survivor's pension is reduced` MEANS
    IF     (NOT `an agreement under section 80 provides otherwise`)
       AND `the person receives a retirement pension and a survivor's pension under this Act, and the survivor's pension is reduced from its full amount under subsection 58(2)`
       AND `the downward adjustment factor resulting from subsection (3), (3.1) or (4)` LESS THAN 1
       AND `the Pension Index for the year in which the survivor's pension is reduced` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN JUST (((`the basic monthly amount of the retirement pension calculated in accordance with subsection (1) or (2)` MINUS `the reduction carried by the Pension Index ratio`) TIMES `the downward adjustment factor resulting from subsection (3), (3.1) or (4)`) PLUS `the reduction carried by the Pension Index ratio`)
    ELSE NOTHING
    WHERE
        `the reduction carried by the Pension Index ratio` MEANS
            `the amount by which the survivor's pension has been reduced` TIMES (`the Pension Index for the year in which the retirement pension first commenced to be payable` DIVIDED BY `the Pension Index for the year in which the survivor's pension is reduced`)

-- src:1109 | (6) If, after a person has reached 65 years of age but before the person commences to receive a retirement pension, a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings takes place under section 55 or 55.1 in respect of that person, the upward adjustment factor referred to in subsection (3) or (3.1), as the case may be, to be applied to any increase in the retirement pension that is attributable to the division shall be based on the time interval between the taking place of the division and the commencement of the retirement pension, and shall not take into account the time interval between the month in which the person reaches 65 years of age and the month in which the division takes place.
@ref Act s 46(6) (src:1109)
GIVEN `the contributor's date of birth` IS A DATE
      `the day the division of unadjusted pensionable earnings takes place` IS A DATE
      `the month with which the retirement pension commences` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
-- Plain gloss: when a division takes place after the contributor reached 65 but before the retirement pension commences, the
-- upward adjustment factor for the increase the division causes is based on the interval between the division and the
-- commencement, and ignores the interval between reaching 65 and the division. The result is that interval in months, at most
-- five years. NOTHING means the division is not between reaching 65 and commencement.
`s 46(6) — the time interval, in months, on which the upward adjustment factor for an increase due to a division after age 65 is based` `the contributor's date of birth` `the day the division of unadjusted pensionable earnings takes place` `the month with which the retirement pension commences` MEANS
    IF     `s 2(2) — the person is treated as having reached a specified age on a date for a provision` `any other provision` `the contributor's date of birth` 65 `the day the division of unadjusted pensionable earnings takes place`
       AND `the month of a date` `the day the division of unadjusted pensionable earnings takes place` LESS THAN `the month of a date` `the month with which the retirement pension commences`
    THEN JUST (min 60 (`the number of months from the month of one date to the month of another` `the day the division of unadjusted pensionable earnings takes place` `the month with which the retirement pension commences`))
    ELSE NOTHING
